BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 559.32 Tm (at 30 or 90 days because direct mail needs three months and probates need a full year [e3YN7RJaj6U @ 01:52:06].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 544.10 Tm (Rick Ginn puts the normal response at one to two calls per 100 pieces, calls three to four months without a deal normal,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 528.87 Tm (and says most people quit at 45 days [WU_DwL7k5ZE @ 00:38:32]. The flip side of slow marketing is slow closings:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 513.65 Tm (the saying on Brent Daniels' channel, voiced alongside Al Nicoletti, is that time kills all deals, and six-month escrows) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 498.42 Tm (invite competing mail, calls and agents onto the same property [wmbh_a5UnqI @ 00:23:51]. Gerry Norton of Flipping) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 483.20 Tm (Mastery TV reports an early deal that took about six months to close, and warns that executors often start marketing the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 467.97 Tm (property before it can be sold, so the operator has to locate exactly where the file sits in the ten-step probate sequence) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 452.75 Tm (before writing terms [K_L_G6jbyAE @ 00:11:25]. Rick also logs a South Carolina basic probate that dragged 2.5 years) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 437.52 Tm (because the lawyer took 90 days to respond.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 422.30 Tm (Paper is where probate deals get killed. Rick Ginn says a two-page contract gets kicked out, so the fix is a long realtor) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 407.07 Tm (contract of four to five pages, and if a lawyer strikes the assignment clause the fallback is a double close) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 391.85 Tm ([LqNx0dBk2f8 @ 00:46:04]. Flip With Rick reports lawyers stripping assignability or demanding a $10,000 deposit,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 376.62 Tm (and says that without price anchoring lawyers push appraisals or BPOs and some have bought deals behind Rick's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 361.40 Tm (back; the counter is anchoring a price like $239,000, a $500 escrow deposit, a lockbox and lawn care with the PR first) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 346.17 Tm ([4-UlN2iP-_c @ 00:10:57]. Rick's minimum anchor deposit is $500 against the lawyer's usual ask of 1 to 2 percent or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 330.95 Tm ($5,000. The full course adds a sequencing trap: share the motion-to-liquidate strategy only after a signed contract, or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 315.72 Tm (the attorney will block it [e3YN7RJaj6U @ 02:06:53]. On authority, Michael Franke warns investors lose probate deals) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 300.50 Tm (by misunderstanding who can sign; an early contract before letters is not yet enforceable, so the operator must sign a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 285.27 Tm (new contract or an amendment re-dated after letters of administration issue [iJVCVwX-rmA @ 00:22:01]. Skip that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 270.05 Tm (re-paper step and the commitment rests on a document nobody had authority to sign.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 254.82 Tm (Economics checks separate a real probate spread from a slow loss. Rick Ginn's carrying-cost math has the estate losing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 239.60 Tm ($25,000 to $40,000 while probate stays open, for example $2,000 a month on the mortgage, which is the pressure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 224.37 Tm (behind the motion to liquidate [LqNx0dBk2f8 @ 00:23:01]. Probate cost itself has to fit the spread: Flip With Rick) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 209.15 Tm (prices a simple probate at $3,000 to $3,500 in attorney fees and $6,000 to $10,000 for a complicated one, absorbs fees) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 193.92 Tm (on huge-profit deals, fronts and gets reimbursed on decent ones, and makes the seller pay on tight ones, calling it risk) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 178.70 Tm (money you have to pay [e3YN7RJaj6U @ 03:12:27]. In the same course, a vacant lockbox house with no buyer inside) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 163.47 Tm (30 days means the price is wrong. The creative-finance trap is the steepest. Rick claims 75 percent of subject-to buyers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 148.25 Tm (get their butt kicked and cites a Florida seller with 64 properties now in foreclosure [e3YN7RJaj6U @ 03:17:51].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 133.02 Tm (Rick's own cure for subject-to default risk is a land-trust reversion clause instead of a foreclosure that costs about) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 117.80 Tm ($10,000 and a year. Chad on Probate Mastery pushes the other direction, saying most of the houses Chad wholesaled) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 102.57 Tm (should have become piggybanks, since wholesale fees are taxed as earned income [AAF69oF79DU @ 00:22:36].) Tj ET
BT /F0 10 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 80.35 Tm (Firsthand probate wholesaling traps and the fixes practitioners use) Tj ET
