BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Every senior-transition operator who spoke starts at the same choke point: legal authority. Sheri Coleman of Florida) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (Realtors YouTube says loved ones moving into assisted living usually designate a family member as power of attorney,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (and if they don't, Coleman's team cannot do anything; many families call, have one conversation, then go silent for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (months while they handle the legal side [yyvDp4R_T84 @ 00:02:35]. Christine of All About Seniors, interviewed by) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (Matthew Cobb, tells families to have a financial and medical power of attorney plus a will or trust in place before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (placement, and to have two years of private pay saved for a community in order to stay under Medicaid [1kkoh35VCho) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (@ 00:00:36]. Dale Corpus splits the authority question into tiers: a senior still of sound mind can sell the home) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (themselves, while dementia or cognitive decline can require a power of attorney or a court-appointed conservatorship) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (to sell on their behalf; if the senior has passed away, the property may need to go through probate before it can be sold) Tj ET
